1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,349
One missed server update cost a

2
00:00:02,349 --> 00:00:04,926
Wall Street trading giant over 460

3
00:00:04,926 --> 00:00:07,200
million dollars in 45 minutes.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,781
A technician manually copied new code

5
00:00:09,781 --> 00:00:10,967
to seven servers,

6
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:12,222
missed the eighth,

7
00:00:12,222 --> 00:00:14,594
and accidentally woke up dead 2003

8
00:00:14,594 --> 00:00:16,128
code called Power Peg.

9
00:00:16,128 --> 00:00:17,208
At market open,

10
00:00:17,208 --> 00:00:19,872
that server fired millions of orders,

11
00:00:19,872 --> 00:00:22,608
racking up 4 million executions across

12
00:00:22,608 --> 00:00:25,632
397 million shares before engineers pulled

13
00:00:25,632 --> 00:00:26,280
the plug.

14
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,516
An internal system had sent 97

15
00:00:28,516 --> 00:00:30,975
Power Peg emails before the open,

16
00:00:30,975 --> 00:00:33,508
but nobody treated them as alerts.

17
00:00:33,508 --> 00:00:35,744
Knight later paid a 12 million

18
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:36,936
dollar SEC fine.

19
00:00:36,936 --> 00:00:39,655
Any automated machine moving real money

20
00:00:39,655 --> 00:00:41,119
needs two guardrails:

21
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:43,002
zero manual server deploys,

22
00:00:43,002 --> 00:00:45,024
and an automatic kill switch.
